erDiagram
    %% E-commerce multi-tenant ER diagram.
    %%
    %% Naming convention: snake_case (English) to match Laravel migrations.
    %% Money columns: suffix `_cents` (bigInteger) — never use `decimal`
    %% for money. Currency is captured per-transaction via `currency_id`
    %% FK + `exchange_rate_snapshot` decimal(18,8).
    %%
    %% Multi-tenancy: operational tables carry `store_id NOT NULL`.
    %% The `BelongsToStore` global scope filters automatically per request.
    %% Catalog (products, categories, brands) is global; per-store
    %% visibility is controlled via `product_stores` pivot.
    %%
    %% Auth: minimal in MVP — users, roles, permissions, password_reset_tokens.
    %% 2FA / passkeys / otp_challenges / recovery_codes / trusted_devices /
    %% login_attempts / security_events are deferred to a future phase
    %% (table is dropped from the schema).
    %%
    %% Customization: minimal in MVP — only `custom_designs` (file upload
    %% per order item) + `order_custom_designs` bridge. The full design
    %% editor (design_layers, print_areas, product_mockups, etc.) is
    %% deferred to v2.
    %%
    %% Shipping: lightweight tracking via columns on `shipments`
    %% (`tracking_url`, `last_event_status`, `last_event_at`) — no
    %% separate `shipment_trackings` table.
    %%
    %% Payments: `payments` is the only ledger; `invoices` has NO
    %% denormalized `paid_amount` / `pending_balance`. Both are computed
    %% via `Invoice::paidAmountCents() = SUM(invoice_payments.applied_amount_cents)`.
    %% No `payment_installments` in MVP — deferred to v2.

    CURRENCY {
